    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 12 October 2005 the single storey detached building, for use as a gym room, store room, washing machine room and dryer and utility room, measuring 10.2 metres long, 4.5 metres wide and 3.53 metres high to top of flat roof (3.76 metres high to top of sky light) was not lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development falls outside the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class E of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the height of the flat roof exceeds 3 metres above ground level.  \r\n"
